  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The clinic</h2>
      <p>Clinique Vétérinaire Univet Saint-Raphaël, at 37 avenue Frédéric Mistral, is part of the Univet network. It treats cats, dogs and small pets and, according to its page, is a short walk from the Bernard Ricci car park. Several team members, vets and assistants, are presented as Fear Free certified professionals, an approach that aims to limit the animal's stress during the consultation, useful for a dog not used to vet practices.</p>

      <h2>What the clinic offers</h2>
      <p>The clinic's page lists general medicine, soft-tissue surgery and elective surgery, dentistry, medical imaging, analysis lab, hospitalisation, nutrition and small-pet consultations. The Univet network adds a shared medical record, payment in instalments and in-clinic product pick-up (Click and Collect). The clinic highlights caring for the animal "throughout its life" and advising its family.</p>

      <h2>Hours and emergencies</h2>
      <p>By appointment only: Monday to Friday from 9am to 1pm then from 2pm to 7pm, Saturday from 9am to 1pm, closed on Sunday (clinic page on univet.fr, read 19/11/2026). In an emergency outside opening hours, the clinic refers you to Univet Cannes Carnot (04 93 99 33 39) or UVD 83 (04 89 88 34 34); it does not provide night cover itself.</p>
      <p>Appointments are made by phone on 04 94 95 93 52 or online from the clinic's page.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: save the clinic's number and those of the two emergency services on your phone as soon as you arrive in Saint-Raphaël.</div>
